[medium] `destroy` currently invokes `cancelImageUrl(url)` without any conditions. It may be worth guarding against `url` being undefined/empty (e.g. on initial render) and, if `cancelImageUrl` has side effects, against cancelling for data/blob URLs or images that have already loaded. A simple `if (url) cancelImageUrl(url)` (optionally adding `if (!loaded)`) would skip needless messaging during ordinary unmounts.

```suggestion
    return {
      destroy: () => {
        if (url /* && !loaded */) cancelImageUrl(url);
      },
    };
```
